The sharpest finding is that execute's wide params: Value signature is not a loophole — the schema is the gate, so an unadvertised field is never populated. And ToolMiddleware, the most plausible seam, is a different mechanism (it vetoes the child's calls at runtime; it doesn't remove a tool from the list).

I kept it open deliberately. The probe answers whether building is possible from here — it builds nothing and closes no gap. Closing it would claim the composition gap is resolved when no production line moved.

